{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon","id":1519823,"title":"A Trinity Space Opera game set centuries post Aeon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-04T20:03:56-07:00","id":1519823,"title":"A Trinity Space Opera game set centuries post Aeon","content":"This thread is for speculations and preferences about a Space Opera game in the <b>Trinity </b>continum centuries after the <b>Aeon </b>game's setting. <br /> <br /> Please be polite. Just because someone's ideas don't please you it's rude to attack. Besides, it could get the thread locked and spoil our fun.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T20:29:04-07:00","id":1519824,"title":"","content":"One thing I think is vital for this game is the ability to play each of the types of inspired PCs.<br /> <br /> Figures like Northwest Smith, Barbarella, Captain Kirk, Barbara Wright, C'Mell, Han Solo, Flash Gordon, and Dune's Mentats, are all Talents (Barbara is listed as a stand in for large numbers of the Doctor's Companions).<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Spock, Councilor Troi, Luke Skywalker, the Jedi mainly, the Lensmen, Guild Navagators, and the Bene Gessirit, are all either Psions or Psiads (or something more powerful we'll call Psychics). Let's call this category Psis.<br /> <br /> Novas/Stalwarts/Olympians are represented by figures like the Doctor, Odo, Data, the Green Lantern Core, Paul Antredies, and several members of the Guardians of the Galaxy.<br /> <br /> The Space Opera game setting will need to support all types and have a practical mechanism for stating the power levels and managing it.<br /> <br /> Figures like Sarah Jane Smith, Dr. McCoy, Dale Arden, Northwest Smith, and others are on a very low power scale compared to figures like Odo or a Guild Navagator. But they still influenced the course of events. Something needs to balance things out so that figures like Jo Grant and the Red Lensman can exist in the same story and both have serious effects on the outcome.<br /> <br /> It strikes me that the dramatic editing systems would be the right sort of mechanism for achieving this balance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-05-2023, 08:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T20:35:19-07:00","id":1519825,"title":"","content":"If we use the term &quot;<b>Talents&quot; </b>to cover types like Daredevils, Champions, Squires, etc. Maybe types like Oracles, Mesmerists, Psiads, and Psions, could all be <b>Psis. </b>Then perhaps Olympians, Stalwarts, Novas, etc, could be <b>Quantums</b>.<br /> <br /> The <b>bold </b>names would cover power categories not power levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T01:05:48-07:00","id":1519831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1519825#post1519825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we use the term &quot;<b>Talents&quot; </b>to cover types like Daredevils, Champions, Squires, etc. Maybe types like Oracles, Mesmerists, Psiads, and Psions, could all be <b>Psis. </b>Then perhaps Olympians, Stalwarts, Novas, etc, could be <b>Quantums</b>.<br /> <br /> The <b>bold </b>names would cover power categories not power levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>1st edition had pseudo-scientific names for them; <b>paramorphs</b>, <b>psychomorphs </b>and <b>eximorphs </b>respectfully. Because the settings do tend to group these things by &quot;power source&quot; it isn't that hard to do.<br /> Regardless, I do like the idea of grouping the character types. Human only for now.<ul><li>Inspired Paramorph (Flux): Talents, Daredevils, Squires, Champions, Assassins</li> <li>Noetic Psimorph (Psi): Psions, Psiads, Mesmercists, Oracles</li> <li>Quantum Eximorph: Stalwarts, Superiors, Novas/Aberrant, Olympians</li> </ul>Non-exhaustive list obviously; Gogs and Magogs aren't placed yet.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> I consider Magogs to have more Quantum than Flux in their Aether (thus would be eximorphs/Quantums) but I'd say Gogs lean more towards the Inspired/paramorph side, even if their Aether is close to a 50/50 mix.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A better question is if all these character type variations are present in this setting, the question is why? Where did the Ambrosia and Aether come from? How did these people decide to work together? What are the threats/antagonists in the setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 08-05-2023, 07:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T02:47:46-07:00","id":1519834,"title":"","content":"I'd be inclined to make this setting something of a kitchen sink, fitting as much as possible from as many previous eras as possible. And yes, that includes Ambrosia and Aether, though they likely go by different names in this era. It should even include cybernetics, digital intelligence, and virtual reality a la Anima.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say that all of these things should be available everywhere. Anima technology, for instance, is probably being used by aliens rather than humans. In fact, I'm figuring that one of the new alien types in this era should be a collective of post<s>humans</s>aliens that have abandoned physical form and moved into a digital existence, interacting with \u201cmeatspace\u201d with robotic drone bodies not unlike the Qin Biosuits (but hardtech rather than biotech). And since even Aegis-era Super-Science is capable of making constructs that are thinking, reasoning creatures, robots in the Space Opera setting should be no problem at all; the only difficulty is figuring out where they fit into the setting.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Aether should be somewhat localized in where it appears, and should be a warning sign of extradimensional incursions, most likely by the Ascendancy. Gogs and Magogs should be possible in these incursion zones (bearing in mind that since we're dealing with an interstellar scale, and probably a galactic one, a \u201czone\u201d can include an entire star system) and are generally seen as harbingers of the Ascendancy, especially since the Ascendancy now knows about Aether and actively seeks to use it themselves: 31st century Squires, Gogs, and Magogs are very likely to be aliens from the Ascendancy.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">At the time of this writing, we're still a ways away from knowing the secrets of Ambrosia (the Aegis KS is still underway); but I suspect that Ambrosia could be recast as a \u201cwonder drug\u201d that enhances the Inspired, and can turn baselines into Inspired. It should be rare, though; although I'm not yet sure what the limiting factor will be that defines its rarity: that will come once we know what the Setting Secrets are for Aegis. Note that Champions aren't <i>just</i> Talents; they're Talents who have been affected by Ambrosia, and as a result can do more. Again, as of this writing we're haven't yet seen Aegis's Gifts; so we don't know entirely what that means. But we <i>have</i> seen the \u201cSpecial Rules\u201d chapter, and it includes added uses for Dramatic Editing for Champions who have access to Ambrosia. The existing rules please this in terms of the Moirai; but in the space opera setting, I could see recasting those in terms of the types of Facets: Clotho benefits would become Intuitive benefits; Lachesis benefits would become Reflective benefits; and Atropos benefits would become Destructive benefits.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> \u00c6on, of course, contributes its aliens to the mix, among other things. This includes the Biosuits of the Qin and the alternate \u201cTalent Gifts\u201d of the Coalition Phyla. And it also adds Superiors to the mix, as well as providing the rules basis for Psiads and Psions.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which: advancing the setting to the 31st century would allow Psiads to evolve further than they have even in the \u00c6on era; and I suspect that the confrontation with the Doyen will likely be long over by then, with one side benefit being that Prometheus Chambers will not longer have Doyen-imposed limitations. It may be, in fact, that the distinction between Psiads and Psions is now strictly a matter of whether they came by their psionics naturally or had it induced in them. Either way, remember that Quantakinesis is humanity's birthright: human psis should universally have access to it, though many may not bother to develop it beyond its basic abilities. Thought should also be put into how or if Oracles and Mesmerists get included.<br /> <br /> Talents, of course, will have Inspiration; but the space opera Talents might have a further ability to \u201cpay for\u201d Dramatic Editing with <i>successes from appropriate skill rolls</i>, similar to the option presented in Assassins (\u201cRolled Flashbacks\u201d, p.103). Also from Assassins is the possibility of cooperative Dramatic Edits (\u201cGroup Flashbacks\u201d, p.102; the text suggests that such Dramatic Editing has the potential to be overpowered and might need limits placed on it; consider requiring every participant to spent Inspiration, <i>and</i> for the group as a whole to spend Momentum on it.) And there may be \u201cDramatic Editing Edges\u201d available to Space Opera Talents that define uses for Dramatic Editing that are cheaper than usual (see \u201cFree Flashbacks\u201d, Assassins p.102 for what to do if the cost of a Dramatic Edit gets reduced to zero).<br /> <br /> I was also going to address Quantum-powered space opera heroes; but I need to leave for work. So I'll come out l back to this later. \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T03:16:28-07:00","id":1519835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1519831#post1519831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1st edition had pseudo-scientific names for them; <b>paramorphs</b>, <b>psychomorphs </b>and <b>eximorphs </b>respectfully. Because the settings do tend to group these things by &quot;power source&quot; it isn't that hard to do.<br /> Regardless, I do like the idea of grouping the character types. Human only for now.<ul><li>Inspired Paramorph (Flux): Talents, Daredevils, Squires, Champions, Assassins</li> <li>Notetic Psimorph (Psi): Psions, Psiads, Mesmercists, Oracles</li> <li>Quantum Eximorph: Stalwarts, Superiors, Novas/Aberrant, Olympians</li> </ul>Non-exhaustive list obviously; Gogs and Magogs aren't placed yet.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> I consider Magogs to have more Quantum than Flux in their Aether (thus would be eximorphs/Quantums) but I'd say Gogs lean more towards the Inspired/paramorph side, even if their Aether is close to a 50/50 mix.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A better question is if all these character type variations are present in this setting, the question is why? Where did the Ambriosia and Aether come from? How did these people decide to work together? What are the threats/antagonists in the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gogs and .Magogs exist somewhere between Quantum and Flux, because Aether involves a kind of blending of the two. Similarly, there might be other as yet on revealed blending of flux and PSI, or even of quantum and psi. That's just speculation at this point, though, and both where it comes from and how it works would need to be worked out. I would be inclined to say that the former pairing should feature the equivalent of force users, defined by a combination of a talent's Skill-based Gifts and a psi's mentalist powers; though I'm not sure how that would be different from a mesmerist. <br /> <br /> The latter, I see being a consequence of humanity's quantakinetic birthright, and therefore something unique to humanity. At a minimum, it should involve a mix of Quantum and Noetic abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T04:08:43-07:00","id":1519838,"title":"","content":"I love the discussion so far.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I would focus my Space Opera largely on Inspired level characters, so basically the same 3 of Adventure! and Aegis for balance sake.<br /> <br /> On a thematic level, I would make Talents partially aware of the nature of their powers, like the Mentats of dune, they have powers (mental powers) but they work as a technique learned at school and not a super power (like Quantum and Psi Powers), so they are aware they are more than human, but to them its because they trained a lot with the proper method, and not the use of an external force (Flux). But not all talents are aware or use this kind of power.<br /> <br /> On a more mechanic approach, I would use the system I created in Fists of Flux Revised (and I love this system, absolutelly proud of it, if you bought FoF its already there, just download the new version) of Stances and Techniques. A Mentat, while in the &quot;Mentat Stance&quot; (I cant remember the name of the trance they enter when doing their thing) they can use some mental techniques to remember a lot of things and do super fast calculations.<br /> <br /> Psis and Quantum should use less dramatic edition, but have access to more powerful gifts than the ones in Adventure! (probably in the level of Aegis, the chapter has not been available by the time I wrote this) with more scale and versatility to compensate the lack of DE.<br /> <br /> On Aliens, I defintly would work aliens as variations of humans, because Space Operas dont have weird aliens, but green or blue people that the main protagonist can kiss (and have brief romances). But as Aeon already have the alien aliens (that are far better by the humans with makeup version), we may need to deal with it, maybe make the human aliens human colonies that evolved for a few centuries, since the Aberrant War, into slightly different humans.<br /> <br /> Next, on Androids (because full robots are not space opera enough) we may use the Quantum Gifts to work as equipments and enhancements on the original model (human level androids), or optionally create a new set of Edges that work like the Cybernetics of Anima, but exclusive to Androids, and they dont have Inspiration (or maybe there are normal androids and Inspired Androids, like Andrew the bicentenial man).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T04:35:11-07:00","id":1519840,"title":"","content":"I'm all for the widest possible variety of types in this Space Opera setting (<b>Aeon </b>is also a Space Opera, but more restricted options work for that game). <br /> <br /> I agree with MATEUS LUS that something like either the daredevil/mesmerist/stalwart set up of <b>Adventure! </b>or the champion/oracle/olympian set up of <b>Aegis </b>will suit this game. I'd add a section in the appendix explaining how to bring in all other printed types.<br /> <br /> Certainly Flux based types, or rather those most easily translated into Flux based types, are the most common protagonists in this type of space opera. With notetic a distant second and quantum lagging behind. But games aren't novels and maybe I'd prefer being Brainiac 5 or Monel to being Han Solo or Spock in a given game. <br /> <br /> The reason I prefer the name <b>Argosy</b> for this setting is the idea of sailing beyond one's cultural ecumen. I want a big mysterious galaxy that a single being can't know or fully comprehend. Billions of inhabited worlds most of which are as complex and complicated as contemporary Earth. Like Sinbad, Ulysses, Gulliver, or Saint Brendan, the PCs should voyage into unknowable mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T04:55:35-07:00","id":1519843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1519835#post1519835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gogs and .Magogs exist somewhere between Quantum and Flux, because Aether involves a kind of blending of the two. Similarly, there might be other as yet on revealed blending of flux and PSI, or even of quantum and psi. That's just speculation at this point, though, and both where it comes from and how it works would need to be worked out. I would be inclined to say that the former pairing should feature the equivalent of force users, defined by a combination of a talent's Skill-based Gifts and a psi's mentalist powers; though I'm not sure how that would be different from a mesmerist.<br /> <br /> The latter, I see being a consequence of humanity's quantakinetic birthright, and therefore something unique to humanity. At a minimum, it should involve a mix of Quantum and Noetic abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal head-canon is that the Adventure! side splats (Mesmercists, Stalwarts and to a lesser extent Daredevil) are a mix of all three power sources but as the background Telluric energy fades, they fall back into the more traditional divisions (Talent, Nova and Psiad). It is explicitly NOT canon according to the Devs. I think it came up a lot, so officially there is no difference between a Stalwart and a Nova...<br /> <br /> Likewise Talents are officially unaware of their extranormal abilities; they think they are just lucky/that good. Daredevils/Squires/Champions know they there is more to it but aren't necessarily in control of them. That is more a function of their era and it's specific inciting incident. Daredevils showed up in the aftermath of the Hammersmith explosion, Squires can and do interact with Aether in ways mundanes can't &amp; Champions are &quot;blessed&quot; after contact with Ambrosia. Assassins are OFFICIALLY the only paramorph that knows about and can knowingly use their abilities. They can and do create strange places that keep other character types out.<br /> <br /> Again this doesn't stop this from not being the case...maybe some archeologist finds records on Squires and Daredevils in some wasteland ruins on Earth and Aeon finally puts 2 + 2 together on the matter and works out how to spot them using a recreation of the 200+ year old science therein. A couple of the surviving Assassin society reach out with an offer to &quot;take care&quot; of some Coalition survivors and triggers the &quot;Talent detectors&quot;. So now they TALK and the obvious conclusions can be drawn.<br /> <br /> Again, I'd like to know more about this &quot;far future, post Aeon-era Space Opera&quot; setting before deciding what these -character-categories look like.<br /> For example if the first AI robot/androids that are fully self-aware were Q-Tech, I'd treat them as cybernetic Novas if they were Gen 1 (created by said Nova), cyborg Stalwarts or Superiors if the later iterations are created by their predecessors. If they were the result of a collaboration of a Talent and a Nova, maybe a cybernetic Magog is more appropriate.<br /> If these Androids were created from say, a psimorph trying to use Electrokinesis, Telepathy and Anima's Glass to try integrate hardtech and biotech in a combat drone that accidentally achieved sentience...well these are going to be psimorphs themselves, through with cybernetic edges built in or as part of their origin paths.<br /> <br /> Aliens are limited to no more than 2 power sources form their &quot;splats&quot;, as this is the official position of the Devs. Humanity is special because we have the capacity to develop all three power sources, and as a bonus we can use the &quot;dirty mixtures&quot; of the power sources. Gogs, Magogs and Quantumkinetics as special &quot;human only&quot; options can be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T05:02:27-07:00","id":1519846,"title":"","content":"This setting is purely speculative. In my mind this vaporware game is set after the year 3000AD. Myself I could be pleased to see the default time period of the game be around the year 5200AD. As far into the future as the traditional date of the Trojan War is in the past.<br /> <br /> This is a speculation thread. Although I love the highly diseplened nature of the speculation so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T08:20:07-07:00","id":1519865,"title":"","content":"I am not excluding the possibility of a Nova / Psion / Talent idea, I just think it doesn't fit the general idea of a Space Opera, as it is more like Cosmic Comics, super heroes in space with armies of lesser super heroes and a lot of weirdos that try to live among them.<br /> <br /> For Novas being limited to lower levels of power we could say they erupted on a lower level of background quantum, and so are less prone to become world wrecking, but also not that prone to Transcendence. You could use the Nova rules, limiting them to Q3 or Q4 too, it would work ok.<br /> Psiads were never that powerful at first hand, and would work ok using the Mesmerist / Oracle rules or Aexpansion rules.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T09:41:29-07:00","id":1519873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1519865#post1519865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not excluding the possibility of a Nova / Psion / Talent idea, I just think it doesn't fit the general idea of a Space Opera, as it is more like Cosmic Comics, super heroes in space with armies of lesser super heroes and a lot of weirdos that try to live among them.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, would we <i>want</i> this to for the general idea of a Space Opera, as opposed to a Star Wars/Legion of Superheroes type of setting? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1519865#post1519865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Novas being limited to lower levels of power we could say they erupted on a lower level of background quantum, and so are less prone to become world wrecking, but also not that prone to Transcendence. You could use the Nova rules, limiting them to Q3 or Q4 too, it would work ok.<br /> Psiads were never that powerful at first hand, and would work ok using the Mesmerist / Oracle rules or Aexpansion rules.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>My preference would be to put the \u201ctypical\u201d power level right around where psions are, buffing psiads and Talents to get them on par with psions, and perhaps nerfing Quantum-powered heroes by saying that Nippon's process for creating Superiors becomes ubiquitous, making honest-to-goodness Novas exceedingly rare outside of a handful of holdouts like Eden (read: generally not available as player characters without explicit Storyguide approval). Though maybe not: if Magogs can coexist in the same setting as Squires, and Olympians can coexist with Champions, why <i>not</i> put Novas and psions in the same setting? <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T10:04:08-07:00","id":1519878,"title":"","content":"Perhaps if Notetic characters could form gestalts capable of powers dwarfing the powers of Novas. And Flux based characters were less disruptive to the setting's hypertechnology. I.e. there's a balance. <br /> <br /> But frankly, if there are transcendent Novas somewhere, in the vastness of the galaxy, what does it matter? Even if the setting's ships can cross the galaxy in a day, throughly searching the galaxy would take millennia. Then add in the ability to travel to other galaxies as easily as 19th century Europeans traveled to Japan. Novas could rule vast interstellar empires without the folks in your neighborhood noticing. <br /> <br /> This would be a vast setting. There would be worked examples, but most of space would be as unknown to the PCs as Australia and the Americas were to the Romans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T10:10:23-07:00","id":1519880,"title":"","content":"I think there should be allegiances designed for a given known space as worked examples. Sure some organizations would be spread out vast distances but these would tend to be superficial. Organizations with real depth would be local, as in they cover a few thousand cubic light years. <br /> <br /> Types and roles would be the important thing. We'd need worked examples and organization templates/archetypes. <br /> <br /> Also a list of allegiances printed throughout the game and ideas to rework them for this setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T10:13:30-07:00","id":1519882,"title":"","content":"In one of the Storyteller Guides there should be notes on crossovers with <b>Scion </b>and both the <b>World of Darkness </b>and the <b>Chronicles of Darkness. </b>Again, these notes wouldn't be in the main book or the Player's Guide. Maybe not even in the main Storyteller's Guide. But somewhere these rules should exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-05-2023, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T10:18:15-07:00","id":1519883,"title":"","content":"I'd actually go for Talents/Superiors/Psiads for the character types. After the defeat of the Doyen the Prometheus Chambers are either jailbroken or discarded in favour of a new way of unlocking noetic powers, and by the time of the setting psions are rare or (practically) nonexistent. Some of the old psi orders are around, but not all of them.<br /> <br /> Superiors meanwhile are a great way to do 'super soldier' type characters, particularly if the technology to make them gets refined enough to have more control over how they develop. You could probably do an entire setting based around Superiors! Plus even in Aeon they've already not exclusive to Japan, it makes sense that in a few hundred years a lot of other factions would have discovered/stolen/bought/leaked the secrets of their creation.<br /> <br /> And Talents are basically a given.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also see roughly two time periods to set such a setting: ~2300-3000ce where humanity is exploring the galaxy and no new big enemies have revealed themselves yet, or far into the future a handful of generations before humanity transcends into ???. For the latter I'd probably pull from stories set just before the fall of civilisation and play up themes of decadence and apathy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T11:21:00-07:00","id":1519889,"title":"","content":"Decadence/apathy isn't really something that Trinity Continuum games tend to do. I'd go with the 2300\u20133000 \u201cera of exploration\u201d idea, with a preference toward 3000 and perhaps a downplaying of the continuing importance of Earth.<br /> <br /> In that regard, I wouldn't necessarily go the route of Asimov's Foundation series where Earth ends up forgotten; but there are plenty of space opera settings where Earth is basically <i>irrelevant</i>: for instance, the Battletech universe, where the Great Houses of the Inner Sphere fight bloody interstellar wars with each other, and where Earth, while literally being at the center of it all, simply isn't a power player; or Traveller's Third Imperium, where Earth exists off in one of the corners of the Imperium and has largely ended up as a historical footnote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-13-2023, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T13:31:23-07:00","id":1519896,"title":"","content":"If you have the ability to settle large areas quickly, which the technology of <b>Aeon </b>would give you, and a society were young couples can settle down and have descent sized homes young, populations can grow quickly. Thus allow a few centuries of expansion and the Earth won't be the center anymore.<br /> <br /> Look at Anglo-America. Britain was massively important in the histories of both Canada and the United States. But ask yourself, &quot;How relevant is Britain to most of the populations of either nation?&quot; In Calgary, Edmonton, Minneapolis/Saint Paul, Denver, Seattle, San Francisco, or Vancouver, is Britain really relevant? North Carolina wasn't settled out of Britain. It was settled largely by groups moving from other parts of the colonies or by groups from continental Europe moving to the lands of the King of Hanover. The areas settled by Scots highlanders being the major exception. North Carolina was the first American colony to declare independence from Great Britain. They did this well before the American Declaration of Independence. Only the Highlanders stayed loyal to Britain.<br /> <br /> If a planet has been settled for a couple of millennia, the cultural importance of the place where the settlers came from will likely be merely historical. Spread humanity out in areas of the galaxy were you can't even see Sol (the sun) through a high powered telescope and Earth becomes as relevant as the names of the Pharaohs of the seventh dynasty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 01-24-2025, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T14:02:08-07:00","id":1519898,"title":"","content":"On one hand I imagine a galactic empire in its golden age ruled by noble houses of Novas, supported by psions and talents, who compete among each other for glory and prestige by expanding the borders of the empire. On the other, you could have a setting in which the empire collapsed due to civil war and now you have multiple factions trying to either rebuild the empire or build something new. In any case, the emphasis in both is that it's a new age of exploration and opportunities where those that become inspired have the chance to decide the fate of the galaxy. When it comes to mechanics I would like to think that by this era the phenomenon of the inspired is well understood and as such they can shape their inspiration however they desire, in other words, I would like to see as many options as possible to personalize the different aspects of our inspired characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T14:24:17-07:00","id":1519901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1519898#post1519898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On one hand I imagine a galactic empire in its golden age ruled by noble houses of Novas, supported by psions and talents, who compete among each other for glory and prestige by expanding the borders of the empire. On the other, you could have a setting in which the empire collapsed due to civil war and now you have multiple factions trying to either rebuild the empire or build something new. In any case, the emphasis in both is that it's a new age of exploration and opportunities where those that become inspired have the chance to decide the fate of the galaxy. When it comes to mechanics I would like to think that by this era the phenomenon of the inspired is well understood and as such they can shape their inspiration however they desire, in other words, I would like to see as many options as possible to personalize the different aspects of our inspired characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I want a vast setting. One that can contain galactic empires, enlightened federations, vast regions of scantily settled space with few authorities, the ruins of vast empires with successor states fighting for survival, and any other type of setting. <br /> <br /> The galactic empire you imagined would make an excellent sourcebook/setting book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T19:18:18-07:00","id":1519919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1519896#post1519896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have the ability to settle large areas quickly, which the technology of <b>Aeon </b>would give you, and a society were young couples can settle down and have descent sized homes young, populations can grow quickly. Thus allow a few centuries of expansion and the Earth won't be the center anymore.<br /> <br /> Look at Anglo-America. Britain was massively important in the histories of both Canada and the United States. But ask yourself, &quot;How relevant is Britain to most of the populations of either nation?&quot; In Calgary, Edmonton, Minneapolis/Saint Paul, Denver, Seattle, San Francisco, or Vancouver, is Britain really relevant? North Carolina wasn't settled out of Britain. It was settled largely by groups moving from other parts of the colonies or by groups from continental Europe moving to the lands of the King of Hanover. The areas settled by Scots highlanders being the major exception. North Carolina was the first American colony to declare independence from Great Britain. They did this well before the American Declaration of Independence. Only the Highlanders stayed loyal to Britain.<br /> <br /> If a planet has been settled for a couple of millennia, the cultural importance of the place where the settlers came from will likely be merely historical. Spread humanity out in areas of the galaxy were you can't even see Sol (the sun) through a high powered telescope and Earth becomes as relevant as the names of the Pharaohs of the seven dynasty.</div> </div> </div> </div>They actually talk about the North Carolina thing in Outlander.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T06:16:02-07:00","id":1519947,"title":"","content":"I still stand by the idea that we need a premise for the setting, then we apply the space opera theme/mood and finally we work on the mechanics to model the new setting. <br /> <br /> Yes, a thousand years is long enough that any polity would likely be unrecognizable. Assuming it even still exists. <br /> Still it may be useful touchstone for players to recognize the game world. It's why most D&amp;D worlds use the English feudal model, despite it being the rarer of the European medieval societies. <br /> <br /> Now a Galactic Empire in a Golden Age with various polities vying for power &amp; prestige sounds like an interesting starting point. Plenty of fertile ground for the stories. <br /> Since we need polities for politicking (and to use as Allegiances), the first question is how many should we have to start with? We can add more as needed. But keep in mind we need to differentiate between them. If we are working with the idea of the Continuum in play, something that is coming up more and more as the gameline goes on, then we could have some backlash/foreshadowing. With some survivors from a timeline where the Civil War has already caused the collapse are running around trying to change the future...to the end of their side winning, of course. It also lets us to use both of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2964_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2964\" data-vbnamecard=\"2964\">Firanai</a>'s ideas as a single setting. Add plenty of &quot;time portals&quot; to cross over between the ruins of the Empire and the height of it's power. Kind of like how Adventure! and Aether have a crossover portal, but we make them a larger part of the setting. Explain it away as the result of damage to the fabric of reality by some superweapon that was used during the war, but no one agrees on who used it.<br /> <br /> I think the Houses of the (Scarlet) Realm from Exalted as a decent model (with easy access) to see how these political Allegiances should look like. That said, Trinity does have it's own archetypes for it's Alligiances within each era settings. There almost always an explorer Allegiance, for example.<br /> <br /> If Inspiration (and all the subtypes) is a well understood phenomenon by this point, at least by the people at the top, then each Allegiance probably has it's own preferences and stereotypes on each of its subtypes of Inspired. That opens ideas for how to play these groupings within each Allegiance.<br /> I'm not fond of the idea of all of them being Noble Houses, but I can see a few moving around. Corporations, religious groups, &quot;regional&quot; and &quot;industry&quot; special interest groups and well....political parties sound like potential options and all of them would have different ideas on how to use those abilities within their ranks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T06:48:37-07:00","id":1519948,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would prefer a exploration era, prior the galatic empire. Nothing against the empire or the post empire era, but There is much more space for exploration (not literaly, as space is expanding) if you still have some lost colonies of aberrants scatered in space. You may have a very interesting period, closer to Aeon, on a post Doyen era, finding new aliens and lost human colonies in many different conditions and tech levels.<br /> <br /> My personal goal would be something closer to the ST TNG exploration level, where you know a lot and have many settlers, with trade between the planets, but still have a lot to explore and a lot of different peoples to met.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T08:52:23-07:00","id":1519958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1519889#post1519889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Decadence/apathy isn't really something that Trinity Continuum changes tend to do. I'd go with the 2300\u20133000 \u201cera of exploration\u201d idea, with a preference toward 3000 and perhaps a downplaying of the continuing importance of Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I probably explained it poorly. I definitely think Trinity can grapple with such themes while remaining in it's 'world of light' position, my core vision would be the PC's theoretical strategic goal is to break the cycle if decadence and apathy and ensure that humanity's on track for some kind of Ascendence rather than a downfall.<br /> <br /> Of course reach to their own, but I'd personally love to see a more optimistic spin on the 'decadent empire' trope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In that regard, I wouldn't necessarily go the route of Asimov's Foundation series where Earth ends up forgotten; but there are plenty of space opera settings where Earth is basically <i>irrelevant</i>: for instance, the Battletech universe, where the Great Houses of the Inner Sphere fight bloody interstellar wars with each other, and where Earth, while literally being at the center of it all, simply isn't a power player; or Traveller's Third Imperium, where Earth exists off in one of the corners of the Imperium and has largely ended up as a historical footnote. </div> </div> </div>Honestly whatever way a space opera setting goes I think the players are going to be unlikely to see Earth. And as a big Revelation Space fan I have no issue with a setting stating that Earth stopped being important centuries ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T10:31:03-07:00","id":1519969,"title":"","content":"The thing I'd be more inclined to borrow from Exalted is the idea of humanity developing \u201csub-races\u201d \u2014 or rather, of humanity diversifying beyond the realistic boundaries of what a human is. If you want to lean into the idea of there being a bunch of \u201caliens\u201d who are basically humans with unusual skin tones or cranial features, why not make them actually <i>be</i> humans with unusual skin tones or cranial features?<br /> <br /> For <i>actual</i> aliens, stick to the guidelines provided in <b>Under Alien Skies</b>; but for these human variations, either make them literally no different from baseline humans besides how they look, or let them pick a mix of minor positive and negative traits to represent strengths and weaknesses they have compared to baseline humans. I also wouldn't go with <i>actual</i> sub-races, per se: they'd be more like family lines, and fully capable of interbreeding with baselines and each other, resulting in more of a spectrum of options than a bunch of distinct species.<br /> <br /> For their origins, consider the possibility that they descend from Quantum-powered humans. They are not <i>themselves</i> Quantum-powered or Corrupted, nor do they show any particular bias toward or against Erupting; but they nevertheless inherit and pass on some of the differences between their ancestors and baseline humans. If Superiors become widespread, then these human variations would most likely be descended from them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-13-2023, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T11:13:51-07:00","id":1519972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1519947#post1519947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still stand by the idea that we need a premise for the setting, then we apply the space opera theme/mood and finally we work on the mechanics to model the new setting.<br /> <br /> Yes, a thousand years is long enough that any polity would likely be unrecognizable. Assuming it even still exists.<br /> Still it may be useful touchstone for players to recognize the game world. It's why most D&amp;D worlds use the English feudal model, despite it being the rarer of the European medieval societies.<br /> <br /> Now a Galactic Empire in a Golden Age with various polities vying for power &amp; prestige sounds like an interesting starting point. Plenty of fertile ground for the stories.<br /> Since we need polities for politicking (and to use as Allegiances), the first question is how many should we have to start with? We can add more as needed. But keep in mind we need to differentiate between them. If we are working with the idea of the Continuum in play, something that is coming up more and more as the gameline goes on, then we could have some backlash/foreshadowing. With some survivors from a timeline where the Civil War has already caused the collapse are running around trying to change the future...to the end of their side winning, of course. It also lets us to use both of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2964_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2964\" data-vbnamecard=\"2964\">Firanai</a>'s ideas as a single setting. Add plenty of &quot;time portals&quot; to cross over between the ruins of the Empire and the height of it's power. Kind of like how Adventure! and Aether have a crossover portal, but we make them a larger part of the setting. Explain it away as the result of damage to the fabric of reality by some superweapon that was used during the war, but no one agrees on who used it.<br /> <br /> I think the Houses of the (Scarlet) Realm from Exalted as a decent model (with easy access) to see how these political Allegiances should look like. That said, Trinity does have it's own archetypes for it's Alligiances within each era settings. There almost always an explorer Allegiance, for example.<br /> <br /> If Inspiration (and all the subtypes) is a well understood phenomenon by this point, at least by the people at the top, then each Allegiance probably has it's own preferences and stereotypes on each of its subtypes of Inspired. That opens ideas for how to play these groupings within each Allegiance.<br /> I'm not fond of the idea of all of them being Noble Houses, but I can see a few moving around. Corporations, religious groups, &quot;regional&quot; and &quot;industry&quot; special interest groups and well....political parties sound like potential options and all of them would have different ideas on how to use those abilities within their ranks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been reading a lot from the new edition of the game fading suns and one key element of the setting is the conflict between the nobility, the guilds, and the church as they scheme and fight for power. Following the theme of the trinity, I was imagining something similar for this setting but more as philosophies: You have the noble houses (or other power groups) represented by Novas who embrace power as a tool for both positive and negative change in the material universe, the psions embrace spirituality and knowledge as a path of enlightenment for every sentient being, and then you have talents who create guilds, companies, and organizations to seek out new frontiers both within and without humanity. However this is just a general idea to start, I'm still thinking about the alliances.<br /> <br /> In any case, for me, this space opera setting should represent the &quot;ultimate&quot; conclusion of the clash between the different parts of the trinity: Divis Mal vs Mercer vs Burano; Nova vs Psion vs talent; hope vs sacrifice vs unity, etc...<br /> <br /> Is there hope for the future? What will be the sacrifices? Can unity be achieved?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T18:12:37-07:00","id":1519998,"title":"","content":"My basic idea for the setting is to have a core setting in the main book (which would get more development in a separate book) and two smaller settings in an alternative setting chapter (these settings would also become books).<br /> <br /> My preferred setting would be in a renaissance/renewal period. The old society was destroyed hundreds of years ago by invaders from an alternate reality. Certain traces of their influence remains. (This allows the introduction of Aether et al later). Society has begun to recover &quot;Hope, Unity, Sacrifice&quot; is the motto of this new Federal League. <br /> <br /> This would be a game involving exploring the ruins of the old society and the new cultures born from it.<br /> <br /> The two alternative settings would be... <br /> First a very Noir/dystopian dark ages/fallen ecumen society. Dictators and corporate states would be major threats. <br /> Second a thriving Federal Ecumen society. An expanding state. It could fall into being an Empire, or the Federal Ecumen could grow into something new and more just than past societies. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T19:35:15-07:00","id":1520002,"title":"","content":"And because the galaxy is so big, all three of these could coexist in the same time period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-06-2023, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T19:38:16-07:00","id":1520003,"title":"","content":"They all sound good, but if we want to play in the setting, we need to commit to an outline at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T19:51:31-07:00","id":1520005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1520002#post1520002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And because the galaxy is so big, all three of these could coexist in the same time period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I saw the first as existing in the neighborhood of Earth. But your preference is key in your game. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T19:54:18-07:00","id":1520006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1520003#post1520003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They all sound good, but if we want to play in the setting, we need to commit to an outline at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well this is a speculation thread (which I hope the Devs read and strip mine for ideas).<br /> <br /> Most of the ideas, while clever, would count as uncopyrightable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T21:27:29-07:00","id":1520013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1520006#post1520006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well this is a speculation thread (which I hope the Devs read and strip mine for ideas).<br /> <br /> Most of the ideas, while clever, would count as uncopyrightable.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Devs explicitly DO NOT look at threads on the fourms to AVOID seeing/using such ideas. Best if we come up with something to use ourselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T08:53:33-07:00","id":1520527,"title":"","content":"I will probably be shun away - but could you all think about<a href=\"https://asimov.fandom.com/wiki/Galactic_Empire\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Foundation</b> series</a> premise?<br /> <br /> There is great Galactic Empire, having now crisis after crisis. Large part of it is still stable ( 'classical Empire' ) but on the outskirts are reformists. And also there are worlds outside of Empire, totally different in polity rulings them. This way you can have literally all three setting variants in one era. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T09:26:26-07:00","id":1520529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1520527#post1520527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will probably be shun away - but could you all think about<a href=\"https://asimov.fandom.com/wiki/Galactic_Empire\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Foundation</b> series</a> premise?<br /> <br /> There is great Galactic Empire, having now crisis after crisis. Large part of it is still stable ( 'classical Empire' ) but on the outskirts are reformists. And also there are worlds outside of Empire, totally different in polity rulings them. This way you can have literally all three setting variants in one era. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you add psychohistory, a predictive social science that gets more accurate the larger the number of people you deal with, then this becomes an interesting struggle of ideas and ideals as well as militaries and diplomatic cores.<br /> <br /> I certainly think a far future Space Opera game ( I still want this game to be as far into the future as the Trojan War is in the past) should have multiple settings in a vast ecumen of worlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T09:31:34-07:00","id":1520532,"title":"","content":"Who needs psychohistory when you have precognition?<br /> <br /> (Answer: Talents, or whatever they've become by this era.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T14:36:47-07:00","id":1520549,"title":"","content":"Is not Psychohistory basiclly Precognition for a large numbers of people? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T16:13:07-07:00","id":1520555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1520549#post1520549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is not Psychohistory basiclly Precognition for a large numbers of people? \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>Precognition is an ability to see the future. If you have a functional psychistory you can form the future. One is based on seeing what is out there to be seen, the other is about prediction as a means to choose what you want to be there.<br /> <br /> An empowered psychistorian would be an epic patron or foe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 09-09-2023, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T16:29:55-07:00","id":1520558,"title":"","content":"The reason I mentioned Talents is that they're connected to Flux in particular, and more generally to timelines. As well, their powers often manifest as ridiculous competence; thus, having their insight/control over the future manifest through a scientific theory hits all the right notes for it to be Inspired Science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T06:30:26-07:00","id":1520663,"title":"","content":"<b>TC: Aegis</b> setting secrets has a couple of elements relevant to this: <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The space station AEON comes from the distance future, even further forward in time than the \u00c6on era. Not all of the space station was thrust back in time. <br /> <br /> The destruction of the AEON could fit into this space opera setting in a manner similar to how the destruction of the Galatea fits into <b>TC: Aberrant</b>: as part of a fourth \u201cHammersmith Event\u201d of immense proportions. Or it could be a more localized one, impacting \u201conly\u201d a few dozen star systems and leaving the rest of the galaxy untouched.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ambrosia is, in fact, nanotech from that future. Which could mean that in this hypothetical setting we're discussing here, \u201cAmbrosia\u201d ought to be ubiquitous.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T02:22:17-07:00","id":1520798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1520549#post1520549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is not Psychohistory basiclly Precognition for a large numbers of people? \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>Psychohistory is basically the idea that as a population increases the actions of an individual average out to nothingness. It's a sound idea, albeit one that probably won't work in the real world. Even in the original trilogy it's of limited use, only one person manages to influence enough people that he throws the course of the future off track (that is of course Hari Seldon via his two Foundations, the Mule has a minimal long term impact).<br /> <br /> Prdcogs though would likely be the second best at it, after Talents, due to being able to build their visions of the future into predictions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T02:24:44-07:00","id":1520799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1520798#post1520798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Psychohistory is basically the idea that as a population increases the actions of an individual average out to nothingness. It's a sound idea, albeit one that probably won't work in the real world. Even in the original trilogy it's of limited use, only one person manages to influence enough people that he throws the course of the future off track (that is of course Hari Seldon via his two Foundations, the Mule has a minimal long term impact).<br /> <br /> Prdcogs though would likely be the second best at it, after Talents, due to being able to build their visions of the future into predictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>He read the book and gave a sound analysis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T05:54:13-07:00","id":1520803,"title":"","content":"To be fair:<br /> <br /> 1. The Mule was a powerful psiad, and the Second Foundation was an Allegiance of psions.<br /> <br /> 2. Seldon didn't change the course of history; his Foundations did. It's revealed eventually that one of the conditions for psychohistorical predictability is that the masses of people being studied cannot themselves know psychohistory, because that creates a feedback loop that screws up the calculations.<br /> <br /> Seldon isn't a precog; he's a Talent, with a Gift for using Science to predict the broad course of future events.<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-17-2023, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T15:01:24-07:00","id":1521540,"title":"","content":"I think we need another term for those Noetic Psimorphs who combine the high power levels of the <b>Psions </b>with the versatility and growth potential of the <b>Psiads. </b> I propose the simple term <b>Psychic</b>. <b>Psychic </b>is a common real world word, and one that is immediately understood. It makes sense that by the time period of this Space Opera game that the limitations of both the <b>\u200b\u200bPsions </b>and <b>Psiads </b>would logically be overcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-28-2023, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T09:06:36-07:00","id":1521983,"title":"","content":"I'd go with \u201cMentalics\u201d, borrowed from Foundation. Likewise, I'd call the Flux-empowered of the age \u201cParagons\u201d, and the Quantum-empowered \u201cAugments\u201d. <br /> <br /> Also: if we go with the notion that what <b>TC: Aegis</b> calls \u201cAmbrosia\u201d is native to this era, there are implications. First of all, there appears to be a Flux component to everything that the nanotech does: <b>TC: Aegis</b> is steeped in hints that Ambrosia-empowered Inspired have a connection to the future, with the heavy emphasis on the role of \u201cfate\u201d in the setting. Recast in this future setting, the <b>TC: Aegis</b> rules for Mighty Oaths could represent a conscious ability of the Inspired to direct the course of the future; and Dire Portents could be reworked as a limited ability of <i>all</i> Inspired to perceive the future. Something like Seldon's Psychohistory could be thought of as this sort of thing on a grand scale: Seldon saw a Dire Portent of the collapse of the Galactic Empire, then implemented a Mighty Oath to motivate that collapse as much as possible and to rebuild civilization as quickly as possible. <br /> <br /> Also, the Olympians of <b>TC: Aegis</b> seem to bear a lot more in common with the Superiors of <b>TC: Aeon</b> than with the Novas of <b>TC: Aberrant</b>: they don't get the same kind of Scale boosts that Magogs can get in <b>TC: Aether</b>, where there are several Gifts that add pone of your Facets to an appropriate Scale; and there's nothing like a Nova's Transformations, a Stalwart's Telluric Burnout, or a Magog's Deviations. For this future setting, I'd double down on that and say that Quantum-empowered Inspired should be Superior-like; Nova-like or Magog-like Quantum-empowered characters need some other explanation for how they got that way. <br /> <br /> And to that end: while most eras have some sort of event that floods the ambient environment with telluric energies, I'd suggest that that <i>doesn't </i>generally happen in this era: the thing that allows the Inspired to become what they are is the nanotech; and a Hammersmith Event would be viewed in this era much like we view Chernobyl and Fukushima. Similar to <b>TC: Aeon</b>'s Flux Zones, these occasional local accidents could be the source of Aberrants \u2014 or they <i>would</i>, if not for the fact that nanotech will most likely have already activated nearly all potential Aberrants as Superiors before such an Event happens. Instead, Novas/Magogs/Aberrants would pretty much have to be creations of Super-Science. <br /> <br /> And that brings up my next musing: just what <i>does</i> Super-Science look like a thousand years from now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T09:39:47-07:00","id":1521986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1521983#post1521983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And that brings up my next musing: just what <i>does</i> Super-Science look like a thousand years from now?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good question. At that point, I'm imagining devices such as time travel machines the size of a bracelet, room-sized reactors powered by the singularity of a black hole, or minuscule machines that alter matter at the subatomic level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T10:44:07-07:00","id":1521989,"title":"","content":"Actually: before you determine what Super-Science looks like, you first need to look at what \u201cordinary\u201d science looks like. And the first thing I'd do there would be to take all of the biotech that's proprietary to the Psi Orders in <b>Prometheus Unbound</b> and make them broadly available.<br /> <br /> I would further expect the Psi Orders themselves to be lost to the past, replaced by newer organizations that fill similar roles without the Psi-specific focus: they should cater to paragons, mentats, and augments, not just (or even primarily) mentats. Part of this comes from the fact that ubiquitous \u201cAmbrosia\u201d renders Prometheus Chambers (and the Nakamura Process) obsolete: anyone who has the potential to be a mentat or augment <i>is</i> one, and long before the various Allegiances have anything to say about it. <br /> <br /> The second thing I'd do for technology would be to look at the various limitations that exist for <b>TC: Aeon</b>\u200b\u200b\u200b technology, and ask if those limitations should be mitigated or even eliminated over the next 900 years. Should the Jump Rings become more like <i>Star Trek</i>'s Transporters? Should Medical Symbionts become noteworthy only in their rare absence? Should IADs still be restricted to single Aptitudes? Should robots still be restricted to SI? Has Quantum-based technology allowed for the development of hardtech equivalents of biotech innovations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-04T08:45:12-07:00","id":1522056,"title":"","content":"I like your ideas Dataweaver! <br /> <br /> So one idea for Aeon is that its like the Jedi Order, a special group working as forces of peace and justice in the galaxy.<br /> <br /> I also think having allegiances be purpose focused and not template focused makes sense. There isn't a Mentat (too close to Dune though) order there is an order dedicated to scholarly pursuits, another focused on warriors, one on politics, one on trade, etc. <br /> <br /> But yeah this is a nifty initial idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T07:10:59-07:00","id":1522299,"title":"","content":"So... Starfield starts sorta where Aeon era ended. It can be also alternative story post-Aeon. Starfield starts where magnetism of Earh in 2150 is killing the planet. So whole humanity move from Earth to new colonise - and rest of S\u00f3l system is kinda backwater. \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> ( Whole SF setting history presentation) <a href=\"https://youtu.be/ISyAhLzKDRU?si=-ve3gkhcF6jUgzXm\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/ISyAhLzKDRU?si=-ve3gkhcF6jUgzXm</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T14:42:10-07:00","id":1522485,"title":"","content":"We'll need something like the Tech Levels in GURPS. It will be important in defining and describing the worlds the PCs visit. Something like the GAMA WORLD System isn't detailed enough. The thirty level system in 1st ed TORG is too detailed for Storypath games. <br /> <br /> The game will likely require tech paths too. A culture focused on biology will have different threats and wonders than a culture focused on chemistry. <br /> <br /> Advancement in other areas will need a terminology too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T04:39:49-07:00","id":1522507,"title":"","content":"We can simply use classical <a href=\"https://kardashev.fandom.com/wiki/Kardashev_Scale_Wiki\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Kardashev Scale</b></a><a href=\"https://kardashev.fandom.com/wiki/Kardashev_Scale_Wiki\" target=\"_blank\"> best is this version</a> - maybe just add some 0.1 to 0.9 examples. Humanity is pointed in 2020s mostly as 0.75 KS right now. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b><a href=\"https://kardashev.fandom.com/wiki/Type_0\" target=\"_blank\">Type 0</a></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><a href=\"https://kardashev.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Type_0\" target=\"_blank\">K0</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Pre-planetary</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Extracts its energy, information and raw materials solely from planetary resources, and can travel beyond its home planet.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b><a href=\"https://kardashev.fandom.com/wiki/Type_I\" target=\"_blank\">Type I</a></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><a href=\"https://kardashev.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Type_I\" target=\"_blank\">K1</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Planetary</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Can use and store the equivalent of all of the energy in and reaching its home planet, and become interplanetary.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b><a href=\"https://kardashev.fandom.com/wiki/Type_II\" target=\"_blank\">Type II</a></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><a href=\"https://kardashev.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Type_II\" target=\"_blank\">K2</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Stellar</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Can harness the total energy equivalent of an entire star's output, and become interstellar.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b><a href=\"https://kardashev.fandom.com/wiki/Type_III\" target=\"_blank\">Type III</a></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><a href=\"https://kardashev.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Type_III\" target=\"_blank\">K3</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Galactic</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Can control energy equivalent on the scale of an entire galaxy, and become intergalactic.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b><a href=\"https://kardashev.fandom.com/wiki/Type_IV\" target=\"_blank\">Type IV</a></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><a href=\"https://kardashev.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Type_IV\" target=\"_blank\">K4</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Universal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Can control the energy equivalent of its home universe, have instantaneous travel, and manipulate the fabric of spacetime.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><a href=\"https://kardashev.fandom.com/wiki/Type_V\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Type V</b></a></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><a href=\"https://kardashev.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Type_V\" target=\"_blank\">K5</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Multiversal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Can escape their universe of origin and explore the multiverse, and have time travel to the future.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b><a href=\"https://kardashev.fandom.com/wiki/Type_VI\" target=\"_blank\">Type VI</a></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><a href=\"https://kardashev.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Type_VI\" target=\"_blank\">K6</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Megaversal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Can exist in an infinite amount of simultaneous multiverses and instances, with unlimited spacetime travel.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b><a href=\"https://kardashev.fandom.com/wiki/Type_VII\" target=\"_blank\">Type VII</a></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><a href=\"https://kardashev.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Type_VII\" target=\"_blank\">K7</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Omniversal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">God-level traveler and manipulator of all universes, multiverses, and megaverses.</td> </tr> </table></div> \u200b<br /> More on KS and newer version of <b>Type 0 - Type V civilistaions</b> on I<b>n a Nutshell</b> video.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rhFK5_Nx9xY\" data-code=\"rhFK5_Nx9xY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/rhFK5_Nx9xY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-14-2023, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T05:26:07-07:00","id":1523011,"title":"","content":"<b>Starfield</b> is showing setting where humanity left to stars - but also billions of people died in the process! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i>'(...) which spurred the first colonization expedition to Alpha Centauri in 2156 and the formation of the United Colonies in 2159. Although the official evacuation continued until 2199, only a fraction of Earth's population was rescued and billions of people perished when Earth's atmosphere was lost in 2203.'</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://starfield.fandom.com/wiki/Earth\" target=\"_blank\">https://starfield.fandom.com/wiki/Earth</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T06:03:57-07:00","id":1523014,"title":"","content":"Kardashev Scale\u200b is a horrible way to measure the tech level because basically all our Science fictions work between 0,75 and 1,25 (Star Wars should be higher as it covers the entire galaxy, but it\u2019s too much of soft SF to be measured in KS, and Star Trek is too energy efficient, so they don\u2019t harvest an entire star energy).<br /> <br /> My suggestion is GURPS or Alternity/D20 Future tech levels with some extra side steps due to Super Humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T08:21:19-07:00","id":1523031,"title":"","content":"Mateus Luz is right about the fineness of detail we need. The Kardashev scale might work for a novel like <b>The First and Last Men </b>or <b>The Starmaker. </b>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bBut RPGs don't work on those scales. The Kardashev scale bearly registers the difference between the technology of Babylon 4000BC and modern day America. We need a scale that can express something like the difference between 1950s America and 1980s America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T04:42:32-08:00","id":1526552,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that with the Ambrosia nanotech in <b>Aegis </b>this future can induce inspiration. Picture a new type of character working at roughly the same power level as <b>Adventure! </b>PCs that can switch whether they use Flux, Psi, or Quantum at will. More powerful characters have to pick one and stick to it, but these characters have incredible flexibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T04:51:37-08:00","id":1526591,"title":"","content":"I strongly suspect that the space station AEON that crashed in Aegis is from a space opera future of the Continuum which will be revealed in the next game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T06:56:17-08:00","id":1526595,"title":"","content":"That's pretty much stated outright in the TC: Aegis manuscript. (All except the \u201cwhich will be revealed in the next game\u201d part.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T07:32:32-08:00","id":1526597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1526552#post1526552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me that with the Ambrosia nanotech in <b>Aegis </b>this future can induce inspiration. Picture a new type of character working at roughly the same power level as <b>Adventure! </b>PCs that can switch whether they use Flux, Psi, or Quantum at will. More powerful characters have to pick one and stick to it, but these characters have incredible flexibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I'd go with \u201cat will\u201d; and Ambrosia <i>does </i>still conform to the boundaries between Quantum, Psi, and Flux. But yeah; I could see ubiquitous nanotech in the Space Opera era leading to the distinctions becoming fuzzy at the low end of the power scale, such that the distinctions between the different categories of Gifts become more guidelines than actual rules. Something like: the Talent equivalent in this setting chooses one category of Gift (Quantum, Psi, or Flux) as a favored category, which he can develop more easily than the others; but, e.g., a \u201cFlux Inspired\u201d would still be able to pick up Quantum and Psi Gifts with a little extra work. Even in Adventure, there are suggestions that the division of Gifts between the different types of Inspired isn't supposed to be absolute. <br /> <br /> It really wouldn't be that much different from how the Inspired can choose which Facets of Inspiration to focus on \u2014 and may indeed be related to that: I've seen a few hints over the years (some of them predating the Trinity Continuum) that the Intuitive Facet is in some ways aligned with daredevils, the Reflective Facet is similarly aligned with mesmerists, and the Destructive Facet is kind of aligned with stalwarts. But these are at most loose associations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T01:28:08-08:00","id":1526660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1526597#post1526597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if I'd go with \u201cat will\u201d; and Ambrosia <i>does </i>still conform to the boundaries between Quantum, Psi, and Flux. But yeah; I could see ubiquitous nanotech in the Space Opera era leading to the distinctions becoming fuzzy at the low end of the power scale, such that the distinctions between the different categories of Gifts become more guidelines than actual rules. Something like: the Talent equivalent in this setting chooses one category of Gift (Quantum, Psi, or Flux) as a favored category, which he can develop more easily than the others; but, e.g., a \u201cFlux Inspired\u201d would still be able to pick up Quantum and Psi Gifts with a little extra work. Even in Adventure, there are suggestions that the division of Gifts between the different types of Inspired isn't supposed to be absolute.<br /> <br /> It really wouldn't be that much different from how the Inspired can choose which Facets of Inspiration to focus on \u2014 and may indeed be related to that: I've seen a few hints over the years (some of them predating the Trinity Continuum) that the Intuitive Facet is in some ways aligned with daredevils, the Reflective Facet is similarly aligned with mesmerists, and the Destructive Facet is kind of aligned with stalwarts. But these are at most loose associations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this idea is roughly how a future setting would work if they ever developed an official one. Quantakinesis shows that humans can manipulate Quantum and Psi together, it's not a stretch to add Flux to the mix. Also from a game design standpoint having three character types running on three wildly different systems is kind of a nightmare. Designing the character type(s) as all using Gifts makes a lot of things easier to run and play. You could sub-divide by focus on type of energy (Flux, Psi, Quantum) through a standard xp discount, or something clever like you mentioned with facets where there are increasing rewards for focusing on one but you're not really locked out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T02:03:15-08:00","id":1526665,"title":"","content":"I would go to a more straight line of All humans are Flux users and have learned how to use flux to control Psi and Quantum, like QK controls Quantum.<br /> <br /> So you have the basic Talent Gifts, the Mesmerist and Stalwart Gifts and some advanced Gifts related to the high end Psiads and Novas.<br /> <br /> To become a high end Nova or Psiad you must focus, so you need many Mesmerist Gifts to be able to get a Psiad Gift or many Stalwart Gifts to get a Nova Gift. If you want to be more flexible you will hardly have any of the high end gifts, but may have basically anyTalent, Stalwart or Mesmerist gifts you may wish.<br /> <br /> Sure, some powerful characters may have enough gifts to have all kinds of powers, but they are exceptions. An starting character will not be able to have any of the high end gifts, for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-17T14:57:50-07:00","id":1532781,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea for a one shot book. After a period of enslavement by the Doyne humanity has revolted and won. Now a United humanity, still spilt by faction and history, must defend what they've won.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-06T07:19:50-07:00","id":1538169,"title":"","content":"Thinking about Earth history shows some possibilities. In 1880 the British Empire was (according to accedemic historians of the British Empire from Britain itself) just past its peak. In the same time period the Chinese Empire was in serious decay racing towards collapse. The Mulghul Empire of India had been conquered by Britain about thirty years prior. The USA, a republic striving to be more democratic, was beginning to understand how powerful they could be. This was actually a progressive period in American history that was beginning to fade into reaction. The Empire of Brazil was collapsing just as it seemed to achieve some degree of promise. Egypt was a colony of Britain and France their ancient ruins sites of mystery, awe, and tourism. The Mayan Empire was being rediscovered. The Ottoman State and Persia (Iran) were struggling to prevent collapse and renew themselves. <br /> <br /> A galaxy half as complex as Earth 1880 would be a grand adventure setting. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-10T15:16:05-08:00","id":1545660,"title":"","content":"A far future setting must be a <b>Yes/And</b> setting. As I described in my massively simplified description above, Earth of the past was, and still is, amazingly complex. Even in the Milky Way galaxy tens of thousands of large interstellar empires or Federations could exist at once unaware of each other. This is a <b>virtue </b>of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-04T11:25:13-07:00","id":1552060,"title":"","content":"Instead of setting this space opera in the far future how about setting it in the distant past? Trinity Continuum: Anunnaki, based on The Earth Chronicles by Zecharia Sitchin, &quot;Gods of the Bible&quot; by Mauro Biglino, and the Eden series by Paul Wallis. 200,000 years ago the Anunnaki/Elohim come to Earth and modify our hominid ancestors creating the Adamites. During the time of the patriarch Jared the Elohim look upon the daughters of the Adamites and notice that they are fair and take them for wives giving rise to the Nephilim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-04T15:17:28-07:00","id":1552061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwolf8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519823-a-trinity-space-opera-game-set-centuries-post-aeon?p=1552060#post1552060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of setting this space opera in the far future how about setting it in the distant past? Trinity Continuum: Anunnaki, based on The Earth Chronicles by Zecharia Sitchin, &quot;Gods of the Bible&quot; by Mauro Biglino, and the Eden series by Paul Wallis. 200,000 years ago the Anunnaki/Elohim come to Earth and modify our hominid ancestors creating the Adamites. During the time of the patriarch Jared the Elohim look upon the daughters of the Adamites and notice that they are fair and take them for wives giving rise to the Nephilim.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a grand supplement. It could also set up <b>Precursor </b>mysteries and Indiana Jones/Northwest Smith adventures in other settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-02T08:25:30-07:00","id":1552832,"title":"","content":"Having shifted my books around to see what I still have. I noticed my Iain Banks books. I remembered that <b>The Culture </b>and a few of their listed rivals occupied a tiny percentage of the galaxy. Moonwolf8's <i>precursor </i>society could still exist in the distant reaches of the galaxy during the whole timeline of the <b>Trinityverse</b> without anyone really noticing. It could be a vast and highly active society while across the galaxy humanity's empires and federations flourished. <br /> <br /> Again, this should be a vast setting full of unknowns and wonders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}